### `declare.*` Namespace
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">
<a name=declare-namespace></a>

A `declare.*` macro is also the **constructor** a [banana block]({{_}}/cmk/banana/#banana-declare) is handed to:

> `declare docker lambda NAME(| .. |)`  lowers to a call of the `declare.docker.lambda` macro with `def=NAME`

A name declared here (a channel, module, polyglot, or single-image container) also becomes a
first-class **[receiver]({{_}}/cmk/compiler/#receivers)** in cmk-lang: once
declared, you can call its scaffolded targets anchorless, with no target-anchor prefix:

> `name.method[...]`

### Worked examples
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

**Stream composition:** macros chain like any shell command:

```Makefile {.snippet .language-makefile}
pretty: ; cat data.json | ${jq} . | ${stream.dim} | ${stream.indent}
```

**Logging with an argument:** a macro call passes positional args:

```Makefile {.snippet .language-makefile}
build:
	$(call log, building ${app_name})
	@# ... real work ...
```

**Keyword arguments:** `mk.unpack.kwargs` powers the `key=value` idiom used by `import.def`, `compose.bind.*`, and friends (full treatment in
[Argument Parsing]({{_}}/argument-parsing)).  One call unpacks a single key (below) or a space-separated spec of many (`, a b=def c='x y'`):

```Makefile {.snippet .language-makefile}
greet:
	$(call mk.unpack.kwargs, ${MAKEFLAGS}, name, world)
	@printf 'hello, %s\n' "${kwargs_name}"
```

**Tempfiles with auto-cleanup:** `io.mktemp` exports `tmpf` and traps its
removal on exit ([details]({{_}}/io.mktemp)):

```Makefile {.snippet .language-makefile}
work: ; ${io.mktemp} && echo hi > ${tmpf} && cat ${tmpf}
```

